userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: The tangent line to a curve at a point P is the limiting position of the secant lines through P and a nearby point Q as Q slides along the curve toward P.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): A tangent line isn't 'the line that touches the curve once' — it's the line the secants rotate into as the second point slides in, which is why the same definition works for a circle, a hump, and any smooth curve.
DEMO STEPS: 6 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

